# Build context for packages/agent-server/container/Dockerfile (built from the
# MONOREPO root so the Node build stage sees the root lockfile + the
# agent-protocol workspace). Keep the context lean: the build stage runs
# `npm ci` itself, so host node_modules/dist must never be shipped (stale
# artifacts + huge context). Docs/git history are irrelevant to the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.gen
.git
.github
.husky
.changeset
docs
**/docs
**/test
*.log
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store
# agent-client never ships in the image, but its package.json must stay in the
# context: `npm ci` refuses to run unless every workspace manifest referenced
# by the root lockfile is present.
packages/agent-client/*
!packages/agent-client/package.json
# container/ runtime artefacts that are NOT baked into the image (the host
# passes seccomp by absolute path at `docker run` time; scripts/md are docs).
packages/agent-server/container/*.md
packages/agent-server/container/run-outer.sh
packages/agent-server/container/smoke.sh
packages/agent-server/container/gen-seccomp.sh
